1. Purpose
This document defines the technical architecture of the Virtual World Platform.

The architecture has been designed to support:

Cross-platform deployment
Large-scale social interaction
Persistent user identities
Avatar customization
Housing systems
Marketplace systems
Age Progression System (APS)
Teen and Adult environment separation
Trust & Safety systems
Future creator economy
The platform is built around a server-authoritative model where all permissions and age restrictions are enforced by backend services rather than client applications.

2. Architectural Principles
Security First
All permissions must be validated by the server.

Clients must never determine access rights.

Safety First
Teen and adult environments must remain logically and socially separated.

Safety systems are part of the architecture and not optional features.

Scalability
Every major service should be independently scalable.

Modularity
Systems should be loosely coupled and capable of being replaced without requiring platform-wide redesign.

Persistence
User progress, property ownership, purchases and account history must survive across sessions.

